12. Since 10/22 ≈ 0.45, the best order is at or slightly below average demand. Going from 1.0 × to 1.09 × the forecast cuts lost sales by about 40 units, worth about 900. But it adds about 115 units to purchases, worth about 1,380, plus storage. So 1.0 × wins by roughly 600 or more.\n\n**Each candidate's order level (product 0 / product 1, × forecast):**\n\n| Candidate | Product 0 | Product 1 |\n|---|---|---|\n| 7 | 1.00 | 1.00 |\n| 2 | 1.00 | 1.26 |\n| 6 | 1.05 | 1.14 |\n| 5 | 1.10 | 1.09 |\n| 4 | 1.15 | 1.14 |\n| 3 | 1.20 | 1.21 |\n\n**Candidates 0 and 1 order every other day.** That saves about 532 in daily order fees. However, stock sits on the shelf an extra day each cycle, which costs about 45 more storage per cycle, so the net gain is close to zero. Their order levels are also inflated: candidate 0 orders product 1 at about 1.15 ×, and candidate 1 orders both products at about 1.10 ×. That costs well over 1,000 in expected profit.\n\n**Robustness.** When demand varies, candidate 7 mainly risks extra lost sales. Each of those costs less than an unsold unit plus its storage. Neither warehouse capacity (276) nor shelf life becomes a constraint for candidate 7."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 3899, "cache_read_input_tokens": 2269, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 3899}, "output_tokens": 5, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-19T01:53:19.060Z", "request_id": "req_011CgAkwr5e1DABndhPnpMbU"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_019xM4wQuRfKSD