1.15 | every other day |\n| 1 | 1.10 | 1.10 | every other day |\n\n**Losses compared with candidate 7:**\n- **Product 1 at 1.15–1.26:** the surplus is about 4–9 units a day. Over 28 days that is 120–250 surplus units at 12 each, plus holding, and the warehouse limit of 276 starts to bite. This costs about 900–1500 more than ordering at the forecast.\n- **Product 0 at 1.10:** about 500 worse.\n- **Candidates 0 and 1:** ordering every other day saves about 14 × 38 ≈ 530 in daily order fees. But a two-day batch adds about 650 in holding costs, mostly on product 0 at 0.9 per unit per day. Partly offsetting that, stock arriving earlier causes fewer shortages. Overall it roughly breaks even, so it does not make up for the over-ordering of product 1.\n\n**Randomness.** Candidate 7 is also the most robust. Its stock stays near zero and does not pile up toward write-offs or the warehouse limit. A shortage here costs no more than surplus does in the other plans.\n\nCandidate 7 has the highest expected profit."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 358, "cache_read_input_tokens": 5807, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 358}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-19T01:56:41.902Z", "request_id": "req_011CgAmECe6dZdDFx4qFkyQ6"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01Mct4UiihJyTAJ7rZT3TFVG", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus