nue plus avoided penalties), and adds about 210 in storage. That nets out to roughly −300.\n   - At ×1.15 the loss is about −930. At ×1.25 it is much larger.\n3. **Product 0 storage is expensive.** It costs 0.9 per unit per day against a margin of only 5. Going from ×1.00 to ×1.10 saves about 560 in missed sales and penalties, but adds about 390 in purchases and about 560 in storage. That nets out to roughly −380.\n4. **The best level is about ×1.03–1.05.** Candidate 7 is close to that. Candidate 6 is at the right level for product 0 but loses about 900 on product 1.\n\n**Ordering every other day (candidates 0 and 1).**\n- This saves 14 ordering fees, worth 532.\n- It costs about 600 more in storage, mainly product 0.\n- Selling across a two-day batch prevents a few missed sales. That helps little here, because with stock this low the leftover units would mostly sell later anyway.\n- Net effect: roughly zero.\n- Both plans also order too much product 1 (×1.15 and ×1.10). Candidate 1 also risks overflowing the 276-unit warehouse around day 26.\n\n**Robustness.** Because unsold stock carries over, falling short is partly made up later, while ordering too much is pure loss at the end. Candidate 7 also uses the least warehouse space, so overflow is never a risk.\n\n**Expected ranking:** 7 > 6 ≈ 5 ≈ 1 > 0 > 4 > 2 > 3.\n\nMy confidence is about 0.6. The gap to candidates 1, 5 and 6 rests on rough estimates of missed sales."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 3942, "cache_read_input_tokens": 2304, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 3942}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-19T01:57:19.905Z", "request_id": "req_011CgAmBFHWWSgMnZKjS